# Video is kept in Git LFS.
#
# It is the only kind of file here big enough to be worth it: the
# transitions example's clip is 2.6 MB, where every other binary in the
# repository — icons, avatars, album art, the route screenshot
# baselines — is under 80 KB. Those stay ordinary blobs, because LFS on
# a favicon buys nothing and costs every contributor a working `git lfs`
# before they can see one.
#
# A checkout without LFS gets a pointer file rather than a video, and
# the transitions example will report that its video failed to load.
# `git lfs install` once, then `git lfs pull`.
*.mp4 filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.mov filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.webm filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
